{"summary":"Corrected alternate binary prefix casing in both integer formatting paths.","explanation":"The `format_test.hash_flag` assertions show `{0:#b}` with `42` produced `0B101010` instead of `0b101010`, while `{0:#B}` produced `0b101010` instead of `0B101010`; the negative `-42` case also had an uppercase `B` where lowercase was expected. The `format_test.format_locale` assertion shows `{:#Lb}` with `-123456789` produced a grouped value beginning `-0B` instead of `-0b`. Both the regular integer writer and locale grouping writer choose the binary prefix with the uppercase condition reversed. Matching the prefix case to `specs.upper()` restores these behaviors while leaving digits, sign, grouping, and other prefixes unchanged.","edits":[{"path":"include/fmt/format.h","old":"  case presentation_type::bin:
    if (specs.alt())
      prefix_append(prefix, unsigned(specs.upper() ? 'b' : 'B') << 8 | '0');
    num_digits = count_digits<1>(value);","new":"  case presentation_type::bin:
    if (specs.alt())
      prefix_append(prefix, unsigned(specs.upper() ? 'B' : 'b') << 8 | '0');
    num_digits = count_digits<1>(value);"},{"path":"include/fmt/format.h","old":"  case presentation_type::bin:
    begin = do_format_base2e(1, buffer, abs_value, buffer_size);
    if (specs.alt())
      prefix_append(prefix, unsigned(specs.upper() ? 'b' : 'B') << 8 | '0');
    break;","new":"  case presentation_type::bin:
    begin = do_format_base2e(1, buffer, abs_value, buffer_size);
    if (specs.alt())
      prefix_append(prefix, unsigned(specs.upper() ? 'B' : 'b') << 8 | '0');
    break;"}]}
